# hw definition for a custom CoreWing F405 Wing V2 variant that adds a hardware
# ToneAlarm (pitched-tone) buzzer on the "LED" pad.
#
# The stock buzzer output (PC15) is a plain GPIO with no timer, so ArduPilot
# tunes only come out as single-pitch on/off beeps. This variant repurposes
# the LED pad - PA8, the board's output 12 - as a hardware tone output: PA8 is
# marked ALARM on TIM1_CH1, which defines HAL_PWM_ALARM so AP_ToneAlarm plays
# the full pitched tunes on a passive buzzer wired to the LED pad.
#
# A tone timer can drive nothing else, and TIM1 also carried output 11 (PB15,
# TIM1_CH3N), so output 11 moves to TIM12_CH2, which nothing else on this board
# uses (outputs 1-10 are on TIM2/3/4/8, the system timer is TIM5, RC input is
# TIM9). Output 11 was PWM-only before as well, so it loses nothing.
#
# Cost: output 12 (the LED pad). The stock board can't run an LED strip on it
# anyway (no DMA stream is left for TIM1), so it was a plain PWM pad. The
# onboard PC15 buzzer output stays; set NTF_BUZZ_PIN -1 to silence an active
# buzzer on it.
#
# Board ID is inherited, so the .apj flashes over the stock bootloader as a
# normal firmware update. See Readme.md.

include ../CoreWingF405WingV2/hwdef.dat

undef PB15 PA8
PB15 TIM12_CH2 TIM12 PWM(11) GPIO(60) NODMA
PA8  TIM1_CH1  TIM1  GPIO(61) ALARM
